 75MN c  Compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC, BNL), May 20, 2026                   
 75MN c  Fragmentation reaction used to produce {+75}Mn isotope at RIKEN        
 75MN2c  facility. Primary beam: {+238}U at 345 MeV/nucleon;                    
 75MN3c  target=4-mm thick Be. Fragments identified by energy loss,             
 75MN4c  time-of-flight, and magnetic rigidity using the BigRIPS separator      
 75MN5c  and ZeroDegree spectrometer. Tof was measured using two plastic        
 75MN6c  scintillators, B|r from trajectory reconstructions using               
 75MN7c  position-sensitive parallel plate avalanche counters, and |DE          
 75MN8c  using a multisampling ionization chamber (MUSIC).                      
